    "result": "**Fixed!** The issue was floating-point precision errors in the price conversion. When JavaScript multiplies `39.95 * 100`, it gets `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`, which failed the validation check.\n\nI've fixed all three price conversion functions by wrapping the multiplication with `Math.round()`:\n- `parseEuros()` in **money.js** (main issue)\n- `cellCents()` in **money.js** (for CSV imports)\n- `decimalCommaToCents()` in **locale.js** (for European format)\n\nThe fix is tested and working \u2014 you can now add prices like 39.95, 19.99, 4.99, 0.99, and any other decimal price without the \"whole cents\" error. Would you like me to commit these changes?",
